# General rules

- Read docs/README.md, docs/architecture/overview.md and docs/RULES.md before writing code. The uppercase docs in docs/ are the target spec (API.md is the HTTP contract); the subfolders describe the code as built.
- An API change updates docs/API.md and re-exports docs/api/openapi.json (`python scripts/export_openapi.py`); CI fails on drift.
- Python 3.12+, Pydantic v2, SQLAlchemy 2.0, type annotations.
- Reuse existing components; do not duplicate logic. Keep functions small.
- Do not modify unrelated files. Small, focused, verified commits.
- Cite only benchmark numbers that exist in experiments/results/latest/summary.md or summary.json.
